		summary = "A **festival** is an event celebrated by a community and centred on one or more characteristic aspects of its religion, [[Tradition|traditions]] or [[Culture|cultures]]. It is often observed as an indigenous or national [[Holiday|holiday]], a religious celebration, or a cultural fair (mela). A festival is a typical case of glocalization, and also reflects the high culture-low culture interrelationship. In addition to religion and [[Folklore|folklore]], a significant source for festivals has been [[Agriculture|agriculture]]. Since, food is such an essential resource, many festivals are associated with [[Harvest|harvest]] time.",
