		summary = "**Filmmaking**, or **film production**, is the process of creating a motion picture. Traditionally, filmmaking is thought of as a process specific to the creation of feature films; however, its iconic methodology has been used in the creation of other types of filmed products, including movies and episodic series for [[Streaming media|streaming]] and network [[Broadcasting|broadcasting]], commercials and advertisements, [[Animation|animations]], [[Music video|music videos]], and [[Documentary film|documentaries]]. The process is nonlinear, in that the filmmaker typically shoots the script out of sequence, repeats shots as needed, and puts them together through editing later.",
